9-30-26:
    ✔ Build Restock + Stock pages (screens/Restock.dc.html, screens/Stock.dc.html) — stock items are user-defined per the live design, and Restock creates new ones @done(26-10-01 14:41)
        ✔ 1. Decisions: decided 2026-09-30 — one StockItem collection for everything (name, unit kg/L/pcs, quantity, lowStockThreshold), user-defined per the design; auto-deduction rules are stored as data on each item, not in code: usedPerPiece (taken per churro piece in an order) and usedPerOrder (taken once per order), both default 0 = never auto-deducted (for things too hard to count, like dips/toppings) — so making a new item auto-deduct later is just editing two numbers, no code change; Churro/Stick/Box are seeded with usedPerPiece 1/1/0 and usedPerOrder 0/0/1, no special key, and can be edited/deleted like any other item; this replaces CLAUDE.md's fixed churro/stick/box Stock and per-type RestockLog; scope of this task = Restock form + Stock page (item list with Low badge + Restock log), Edit restock entry / Edit stock item / the actual deduction are separate tasks below; decided 2026-09-30 (answers to the open questions): (a) names match trimmed + case-insensitively, so "flour " tops up "Flour" and the stored name keeps its first spelling; (b) once a typed name matches an existing item, the Unit select switches to that item's unit and is disabled, and the server also rejects a mismatched unit (400) as a backstop; (c) items created from Restock start with lowStockThreshold 0 — and since the design's "Low when quantity < threshold" would never flag an empty item at 0, an item at quantity ≤ 0 always shows a separate red "Out" badge (danger colors, not in the design), while quantity < threshold shows the design's peach "Low" badge; ≤ 0 rather than === 0 because auto-deduction may later push a count below zero; (d) churro restocks are typed freely like every other item — no packs-of-50 special case; (e) the Stock page shows the 20 most recent restock-log entries (the server limits it, so the 7s poll never reloads the whole history) @done(26-09-30 15:11)
        ✔ 2. Server: models/stockItemModel.js — name (required, trimmed, unique case-insensitively via a collation index with strength 2 — per 1a — so two phones can't both create "Flour"), unit (enum kg/L/pcs), quantity (Number, decimals allowed e.g. 1.5 kg, no min on purpose — auto-deduction may push it below 0 and a later save() must not fail; the Out badge covers it), lowStockThreshold (Number, default 0, min 0 — per 1c), usedPerPiece / usedPerOrder (Number, default 0, min 0) — plus a findByName(name) static that trims and applies the same collation, so no lookup can forget it and miss "Flour" when given "flour" @done(26-09-30 15:19)
        ✔ 3. Server: models/restockLogModel.js — stockItem (ObjectId ref), quantity (> 0), unit copied at restock time (so an old entry still reads right if the item's unit changes later), staffMember (Jui/Impact, set by the server from req.user.name like createOrder), timestamps: true (for "Today, 9:12 AM") — quantity must be > 0 (validator, since min: 0 would let 0 through); the unit and staff enums now live in server/constants/units.js and constants/staffMembers.js, shared with StockItem and Order so a new unit or a third person is one change @done(26-09-30 15:37)
        ✔ 4. Server: scripts/seedStock.js — creates Churro / Stick / Box (unit pcs, their usedPer* values) only if missing; same idempotent style as seedAccount.js; run once against Atlas — ran 2026-10-01: Churro / Stick / Box (pcs, quantity 0, lowStockThreshold 20/50/20 — Jui's values, usedPerPiece 1/1/0, usedPerOrder 0/0/1) are in Atlas, all three show Out until their first restock; a second run skipped all three; awaits StockItem.init() so the unique name index exists before the first insert; note: server/scripts/ is gitignored (same as seedAccount.js), so this file isn't in the repo @done(26-10-01 13:06)
        ✔ 5. Server: GET /api/v1/stock-items (every item, sorted by name) and GET /api/v1/restocks (the 20 newest per 1e, populate the item's name), both behind protect — stockItemController.getAllStockItems uses a new findSortedByName() static (same collation as the index, so names sort A–Z regardless of case instead of capitals-first); restockController.getRecentRestocks limits to 20 and populates only the item name; both routers are already mounted in app.js (moved here from step 7 so this could be tested); checked: Atlas returns Box, Churro, Stick and 0 restocks, and both URLs answer 401 without a token @done(26-10-01 13:11)
        ✔ 6. Server: POST /api/v1/restocks { name, quantity, unit } — find the item by name with the same case-insensitive collation (1a) or create it with threshold 0 (1c); 400 if the item exists with a different unit (1b), raise its quantity with findOneAndUpdate +  (atomic — not read-modify-write, since both phones can restock at the same time), then create the log entry; staffMember from the token — quantity/unit are validated with the RestockLog schema before any write (so a 0 never leaves an empty new item behind); a concurrent create of the same new name (E11000) falls back to the item the other phone just made; the log is written before the $inc (a log whose amount wasn't added is visible and fixable, an unlogged count change isn't); uses returnDocument: 'after' (Mongoose 9 deprecated { new: true }); tested against Atlas with throwaway ZZ items, then removed: new name creates, "  zz test item " + "2.5" tops up to 7.5, wrong unit → 400 with no change, quantity 0 → no item created, missing name → 400, two simultaneous restocks of a new name → 1 item, quantity 7, 2 log entries @done(26-10-01 13:24)
        ✔ 7. Server: (routers already mounted in step 5) Postman: GET /stock-items lists the 3 seeded items, GET /restocks starts as []; a new name creates an item; an existing name tops it up; two restocks of the same item add up; quantity 0 / negative / a unit outside kg-L-pcs is rejected @done(26-10-01 13:42)
        ✔ 8. Client: Restock.jsx replacing the stub — SubPageShell (back → /stock, per the design); Item name text input + <datalist> of existing names from GET /stock-items; helper text "Type an existing item to top it up, or a new name to start tracking it."; Quantity (type=number, inputMode=decimal) and Unit select side by side — when the typed name matches an existing item (trimmed, case-insensitive), set Unit to that item's unit and disable the select (1b); all inputs ≥16px (the mockup's 15px is the known bug); "Add restock item" primary button → POST, then navigate to /stock; server errors inline like NewRound — decided 2026-10-01: the help text says what will happen ("Topping up Flour — 8 kg in stock now." / "New item — it will start being tracked.", the design's sentence while empty) so a typo can't silently start a second item; a new item's Unit starts unpicked ("Unit…", required) because it's locked for good once created; name matching uses findItemByName in src/constants/stock.js (localeCompare with sensitivity: accent = the server's collation strength 2), the shown unit is derived each render, quantity has step="any" so 1.5 kg is accepted; errorMessage() moved to src/api.js (EditOrder uses it too) @done(26-10-01 14:21)
        ✔ 9. Client: Stock.jsx replacing the stub — AppShell subtitle "Stock · N items, M low"; "Restock" primary link button; items card: name + "8 kg", or a badge instead of the plain amount: red "Out" when quantity ≤ 0, else peach "Low" (warning icon, same look as the Pending badge) when quantity < lowStockThreshold (1c); subtitle's "M low" counts both; "Restock log" section: "Flour +5 kg" (amount in green) over "Today, 9:12 AM · Jui"; rows link to /stock/:id and /restocks/:id stub routes for now; 7s polling (usePolling) so both phones see restocks — built: the Out badge reads "Out" (red, StockBadge level="out") instead of a number, since a count can go below 0 once orders deduct stock, while Low keeps the design's amount ("1.5 kg"); the rule lives in stockLevel() and the row's right side in components/StockLevel.jsx, both ready for Home in step 10; LowStockBadge was renamed StockBadge with a level prop; formatAmount / formatLoggedAt ("Today, 9:12 AM" / "Yesterday, …" / "Sep 26") added to constants/stock.js; empty states (not in the design): "No stock items yet — tap Restock to start tracking one." and "No restocks yet."; a log row whose item is gone shows "Deleted item" as a placeholder until that open question is decided; EditStockItem / EditRestock are "Coming soon" stubs at /stock/:id and /restocks/:id @done(26-10-01 14:31)
        ✔ 10. Client: Home's StockPreview — replace the hardcoded STOCK_PREVIEW in Home.jsx with GET /stock-items and the same Out/Low rule as Stock — put that rule in one shared helper so Stock and Home can't disagree (decide how many items Home shows, or only the Out/Low ones) — decided 2026-10-01: Home shows at most 5 items, Out first, then Low, then the rest (each group A–Z, kept from the server's order because Array.sort is stable) via pickPreviewItems in constants/stock.js; StockPreview now renders StockLevel, so Home and Stock share one Out/Low rule; the hardcoded STOCK_PREVIEW is gone; stock is polled separately from rounds (own loading / error / Try again), so a failed stock load doesn't hide Active rounds @done(26-10-01 14:37)
        ✔ 11. Test: restock an existing item and a brand-new one from both phones; quantities add up and the log shows who/when; the Low badge appears/disappears across the threshold and Out appears at 0 on Stock and Home; "flour" tops up "Flour" and the Unit select locks to its unit; the log shows only the 20 newest; unit/quantity validation errors show inline; phone width, ≥16px inputs, 44px touch targets @done(26-10-01 14:41)
    ✘ errorController: in development, Mongoose ValidationError/CastError reach the client as 500 with the raw message ("RestockLog validation failed: quantity: …"); only production converts them to 400 + a short message — convert them in both environments (affects every form's inline error, not just Restock); also: when NODE_ENV is neither development nor production (e.g. a script that requires app.js without loading config.env), errorController sends no response at all and the request hangs — add a fallback branch — left as is (Jui, 2026-10-05): it only happens in the development environment, where the raw error and stack are useful for debugging; production already converts them; the forms check their own input first (NewExpense / EditExpense); review again before any real deploy (see CLAUDE.md) @cancelled(26-10-05)
    ✘ Low-stock alerts + a daily summary (from CLAUDE.md's "Not yet implemented", never in the design) — not doing either (Jui, 2026-10-05): the Low / Out badges on Stock and Home already warn about low stock, since both people open the app for every order; Finances' all-time totals are enough, no per-day breakdown @cancelled(26-10-05)
    ✔ Small cleanups split out of the errorController item (not about the dev environment): roundController.closeRound still passes the deprecated { new: true } (Mongoose 9 → returnDocument: 'after'; works today, may break on the next Mongoose upgrade); and switch the remaining inline "err instanceof TypeError ? 'Cannot reach the server…'" copies (Home, NewOrder ×2, NewRound, usePolling) to errorMessage() from src/api.js — done: all five now call errorMessage(), so the message lives only in api.js; Login.jsx keeps its own line on purpose — its bare catch also catches a non-JSON response, and errorMessage() would show that raw SyntaxError text instead of "Cannot reach the server"; closeRound tested against Atlas on a throwaway round: the response carries the ended round (isActive false), no deprecation warning, round removed; client lint + build pass @done(26-10-05)
    ✔ Build Edit restock entry page (screens/EditRestock.dc.html) — name/quantity/unit + Save changes + Delete entry; editing or deleting an entry must also move the item's quantity by the difference ( new − old, or −quantity on delete); header shows "Logged Today, 9:12 AM · Jui" — decided 2026-10-01 (corrected the same day: a first version renamed the item, Jui meant only this entry): editing Item name MOVES this entry to the item with that name — the old item gets the amount taken back, the new one gets it added, nothing is renamed (renaming an item belongs on Edit stock item); a name not seen before starts a new item in the entry's unit, same as Restock (shared findOrCreateItem in restockController); moving to an item counted in another unit is allowed — the entry takes that unit and the page warns "Cups is counted in pcs — make sure the quantity is in pcs too."; the Unit select is locked and follows the name; a note (not in the design) says what Save will do: "Moves this restock from Sugar to Flour."; Delete entry needs two taps like Cancel order; server: GET/PATCH/DELETE /restocks/:id — PATCH validates the quantity before anything is written, saves the entry first, then moves the counts with $inc; delete takes the amount back off the item before removing the entry; SubPageShell gained an optional subtitle for "Logged Today, 9:12 AM · Jui"; tested against Atlas with throwaway ZZ items, then removed @done(26-10-01 14:58)
    ✔ Build Edit stock item page (screens/EditStockItem.dc.html) — name, unit, "Low-stock alert below" threshold, Save changes, Delete item; plus usedPerPiece / usedPerOrder inputs, which are NOT in the design (Jui to decide wording/placement); also the place to correct a count by hand; covers the older "Low-stock threshold" task under 9-19-26; OPEN QUESTION — decide when building this page: once a stock item is deleted, its old restock-log entries point to nothing (populate returns null) — delete those log entries along with the item, or keep them and show the name as "Deleted item"? — decided 2026-10-03: Delete item is a SOFT delete (isDeleted) because the restock log is a permanent record of what was bought — the item disappears from Stock, Home and the name suggestions (findSortedByName filters it) but its log entries keep the real name, marked "(deleted)"; restocking a deleted item's name brings the same item back (count restarts at 0 in the new restock's unit, history continues; done atomically with isDeleted: true in the filter so two phones can't reset each other); renaming to a deleted item's name explains that instead of a bare "taken"; Unit can change with a warning (numbers are read in the new unit, old log entries keep theirs); added "In stock now" (not in the design) to set the counted amount — not logged; added an "Auto-deduct on each order" section (Per churro piece / Per order, not in the design) with a note that orders don't deduct yet; Save sends only the changed fields so a threshold edit can't overwrite a restock made on the other phone meanwhile; Delete item needs two taps; known gap: Restock can't see deleted items, so typing one's name says "New item…" although it brings the old one back @done(26-10-03 15:28)
    ✔ Auto stock deduction on orders — decided 2026-10-03: stock is taken when the order is placed, cancelling gives it back, editing items moves stock by the difference; everything is per serving (quantity), not per order: a regular serving takes S 4 / M 8 Churro + as many Stick + 1 Box, a Strawberry Nutella Bite serving (a box of 10) takes 10 Bite churro + 1 Stick + 1 Bite box; rules are still data on each item — usedPerPiece / usedPerServing (new) / usedPerBite (new) / usedPerOrder (once per order, kept for things like bags, unused now); each order stores stockDeductions (what it took) so cancel/edit give back exactly that, and stockDeducted marks orders placed after this feature — the 10 older orders never took stock, so editing or cancelling them leaves stock alone; deleted items are skipped; utils/stockDeduction.js holds the pure maths + one bulkWrite of $inc per change; seedStock.js added Bite churro / Bite box and moved Box from 1-per-order to 1-per-serving (one-time, only items still missing usedPerServing); EditStockItem shows the four rules and no longer says orders don't deduct; tested against Atlas with a snapshot of every real count restored at the end (cancel alone brought them all back) @done(26-10-03 16:55)
10-5-26:
    ✔ Build Finances + Add expense + Edit expense pages (design: Expenses.dc.html, AddExpense.dc.html, EditExpense.dc.html) @done(26-10-05 14:57)
        ✔ 1. Decisions: decided 2026-10-05 — the three stat cards (Revenue / Expenses / Profit) are ALL-TIME totals, not "this month" as the design's subtitle says (Revenue for all time minus one month's expenses would overstate profit, so all three use the same range) → the subtitle becomes "Finances · All time"; Revenue = sum of totalPrice over every non-cancelled order (same { isCancelled: { $ne: true } } filter as getAllOrders, delivery fees included because totalPrice includes them); the "Recent expenses" list shows the 20 NEWEST expenses of any month (changed the same day from "this month only" — Jui: the cards are all-time, so the list shouldn't be cut at a month either; same 20-newest server-side limit as the restock log, so the 7s poll never reloads the whole history; the list's total won't match the Expenses card once there are more than 20, and that's fine — it's "recent", not "all"); an expense's date is when it was logged (createdAt, "Logged Sep 16 · Jui"), as in the design — no date field; Delete entry is a REAL delete (like Delete entry on a restock — people delete a wrong or duplicate entry, nothing should keep it) and needs two taps like the other delete buttons; the list keeps the design's heading "Recent expenses"; a negative Profit is red (text-danger, Jui 2026-10-05 — the design only shows green), zero or more stays green @done(26-10-05)
        ✔ 2. Server: models/expenseModel.js — rebuilt, NOT restored from af86b78 (the old ExpenseModel.js used `default: Date.now()`, which runs once when the server starts, so every expense got the same time; it also had no staff) — title (String, required, trimmed — the design's "Expense title"), amount (Number, required, must be > 0 — a validator like RestockLog's quantity, since min: 0 would let 0 through), staffMember (enum from constants/staffMembers.js, set by the server from req.user.name like createOrder / createRestock), timestamps: true (createdAt is the expense's date); still deliberately NOT linked to RestockLog (see CLAUDE.md's Expense bullet: gas, rent and delivery aren't stock) — built; Atlas had no leftover expenses collection from the old model (0 docs); checked with validate(): blank title, amount 0 / negative / missing and an unknown staff name are rejected, 12.5 is accepted; two created a moment apart get different createdAt (the old bug is gone); test docs removed @done(26-10-05)
        ✔ 3. Server: controllers/expenseController.js + routes/expenseRoutes.js, every route behind protect, mounted at /api/v1/expenses in app.js (the commented-out lines are already there) — POST / (title + amount from the body, staffMember from the token); GET / (the 20 newest: sort({ createdAt: -1 }).limit(20), same as restockController.getRecentRestocks); GET /:id; PATCH /:id (whitelist title / amount, findById + set + save() like updateStockItem so validation runs); DELETE /:id (findByIdAndDelete, 200 with a JSON body, not 204 — getJson parses every response) — built; POST takes only title / amount from the body (a staffMember or createdAt sent by the client is ignored); tested by calling the handlers directly against Atlas with throwaway ZZ expenses, then removed: create 201 with staffMember from the token, amount 0 / no title → ValidationError with nothing written, list newest-first ≤ 20, missing id → 404, PATCH amount keeps the title and can't change staffMember, PATCH amount 0 leaves the stored value, delete 200 then 404; both URLs answer 401 without a token; known gap until the errorController task: in development a ValidationError reaches the client as 500 with the raw "Expense validation failed: …" message instead of 400 @done(26-10-05)
        ✔ 4. Server: GET /api/v1/finances/summary (behind protect, its own small financeController + financeRoutes) — the project's first MongoDB aggregation: Order.aggregate([{ $match: { isCancelled: { $ne: true } } }, { $group: { _id: null, total: { $sum: '$totalPrice' } } }]) for revenue, Expense.aggregate([{ $group: { _id: null, total: { $sum: '$amount' } } }]) for expenses (run both with Promise.all), profit = revenue − expenses; an empty collection makes aggregate return [] rather than a 0 total, so fall back to 0 — built (financeController.getSummary → { revenue, expenses, profit }, mounted at /api/v1/finances); tested against Atlas: 10 orders, 2 cancelled → revenue 1182 (matches summing non-cancelled totalPrice by hand; 1620 with the cancelled ones), expenses 0 with an empty collection, two throwaway ZZ expenses (450 + 12.5) → expenses 462.5 and profit 719.5, back to 0 after removing them; 401 without a token @done(26-10-05)
        ✔ 5. Server test (Postman / curl with a real token): POST an expense → shows in GET / and raises the summary's expenses; title missing / amount 0 / amount negative → 400 with no document written; PATCH changes only what's sent; DELETE removes it and the summary drops back; summary revenue equals the sum of non-cancelled orders' totalPrice; GET / returns at most 20, newest first; every route answers 401 without a token @done(26-10-05 14:39)
        ✔ 6. Client: NewExpense.jsx (route /expenses/new already exists, Home's "Add expense" quick action links to it) replacing the stub — SubPageShell "Add expense", back → /finances (as in the design, even when opened from Home — same as Restock's back → /stock); "Expense title" text input (placeholder "e.g. Propane gas refill") and "Amount (฿)" (type=number, inputMode=decimal, step="any", placeholder "0"), both from formClasses.js so they're ≥16px (the mockup's 15px is the known bug); "Add expense" primary button (48px) → POST, then navigate('/finances', { replace: true }); server errors inline with errorMessage() from src/api.js — built; also checked before sending (not in the design): a title of only spaces → "Please enter what the expense was for." (the browser's required lets spaces through) and amount 0 → "Amount must be more than 0." (in development the server's own message would read "Expense validation failed: …"); a negative amount is stopped by the browser's min="0"; tested with Playwright at 390px: opened from Home's quick action, inputs 44px / 16px, button 48px, no request sent for invalid input, ZZ 12.5 → 201, lands on /finances, Back goes to Home not the form, saved with staffMember Jui, no console errors; test expense removed @done(26-10-05)
        ✔ 7. Client: Finances.jsx replacing the stub — AppShell subtitle "Finances · All time"; three stat cards in a 3-column grid (Revenue / Expenses / Profit, Profit in green — negative color per 1); "Add expense" primary link button → /expenses/new; "Recent expenses" (20 newest): "Flour & sugar delivery · ฿850" over "Sep 16 · Jui", each row links to /expenses/:id — reuse formatLoggedAt from constants/stock.js for the date (same "Today, 9:12 AM" / "Yesterday, …" / "Sep 26" as the restock log; move it to a shared date helper if importing it from stock.js reads wrong) and ฿ + toLocaleString() for amounts like the rest of the app; empty state (not in the design) e.g. "No expenses yet."; loading / error / Try again; poll summary + list every 7s with usePolling so both phones see new expenses — built: StatCard.jsx (unused since the Home redesign) became the Finances card (text-caption 11px label, text-display-compact 19px value, valueClassName for the Profit color); formatBaht in Finances.jsx writes a loss as "-฿3,868" (not "฿-3,868"); formatLoggedAt is imported from constants/stock.js as is (not moved); the Add expense button stays outside the loading/error states, like Stock's Restock; rows link to /expenses/:id, which is blank until step 8; tested with Playwright at 390px: subtitle "Finances · All time", the 3 cards on one row (110px each, 11px / 19px), revenue ฿1,182 = the summary, "No expenses yet." when empty, ZZ ฿50 added via the button → row "ZZ test · ฿50 / Today, 2:46 PM · Jui" and Profit ฿1,132, a ฿5,000 expense added from a script (as if from the other phone) showed up on the next poll with Profit "-฿3,868" in red; no console errors; test expenses removed; known limit: a 7-digit amount ("-฿1,234,567") overflows its card by 8px at 390px — 6 digits fit @done(26-10-05)
